// l.25278 item 5, l.25355 item 7, l.25383). PRICES OFF PARITY, DEF-754 (LOW, fails closed, made by row B2 with W11's function-value try): a getter
// named as a function value is taken as one that may hand back a view of what it is given, so a right program that names one is refused
// (BORROW-015), while the same program with the call written by name is accepted. Three faces, one case each: W11's `w11_fv2c`, AW9's `aw9_p3gnA`
// (three getters of one type) and W13's `w13_gp3_ok` (inside a generic). Ways out: `fv_getter_def754_wayout_w11_fv2c_d_ok.npk` and
// `fv_getter_def754_wayout_w11_fv2c_bn_ok.npk`, which run 67 on main and on every build from row 4 on. In the form of main's prices files.
